  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Consider equations of the form \\(x^2+bx+c=0.\\) How many such equations have real roots and have coefficients \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) selected from the set of integers \\(\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(19\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(18\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(17\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(16\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "19"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1963-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(c\\) equal to \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(5,\\) and \\(6,\\) the condition \\(b^2\\geq4c\\) permits respectively \\(5,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(2,\\) and \\(2\\) values of \\(b\\) in the given set. Their sum is \\(5+4+3+3+2+2=19.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Real roots require \\(b^2\\geq4c\\)",
        "For each \\(c=1,\\ldots,6,\\) count the allowed values of \\(b\\)"
      ],
